    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2012-p20.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The middle fraction is \\(\\dfrac{7}{21}=\\dfrac13\\). Also, \\(\\dfrac{5}{19}\\lt\\dfrac13\\) because \\(3\\cdot5=15\\lt19\\), while \\(\\dfrac{9}{23}\\gt\\dfrac13\\) because \\(3\\cdot9=27\\gt23\\). Therefore \\[\\dfrac{5}{19}\\lt\\dfrac{7}{21}\\lt\\dfrac{9}{23}.\\]\n\nThus, the answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "Compare the fractions to \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\).",
        "Write each fraction as \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) plus or minus a small amount."
      ],
